course: dictionary
lesson: 11390
title: Abyss: a very deep hole or gap
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «abyss» is a noun. It names a very deep hole or gap, so deep it seems to have no bottom. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they give you clues.
explain: «The torch beam did not reach the bottom of the abyss.» A torch beam that cannot reach the bottom tells you the hole is very deep. Swap in your meaning, "the very deep hole", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Abyss can also mean a huge gap that seems impossible to cross. «The gap between the two teams felt like an abyss.» Here the clue is the word gap, and the sentence is about teams, not holes in the ground.
fact: An abyss is a very deep hole or gap, so deep it seems to have no bottom.
fact: «Abyss» can also mean a terrible situation or a huge difference that seems impossible to cross.
fact: In science, the abyss is the deepest, darkest part of the ocean.
fact: Scientists call the deep sea floor the abyssal zone, where it is cold and dark and strange fish live.
fact: Phrases with «abyss» include «stare into the abyss» and «on the edge of an abyss».
exercise: «The torch beam did not reach the bottom of the abyss.» What is an abyss in this sentence? | A small puddle in the garden | *A very deep hole with no bottom you can see | A tall tree on a hill | A loud noise from far away
exercise: «Scientists sent a robot into the abyss to find strange fish.» Where did the robot go? | Around a football pitch | Into a busy shopping centre | *Into the deepest, darkest part of the ocean | Up into the clouds
exercise: «The gap between the two teams felt like an abyss.» What does abyss mean here? | *A huge gap that seems impossible to cross | A happy song | A small step on the stairs | A sunny field
test: «The hikers stopped at the edge of the abyss.» Where were the hikers standing? | In a warm bath | On a flat, grassy lawn | Inside a cosy tent | *On the brink of a very deep drop
test: Which of these is a phrase with «abyss» from the lessons? | Count to ten | Look at the moon | *Stare into the abyss | Stare at the clock
exam: Ella says an abyss is a shallow puddle. Is she right? | Yes, it is a shallow puddle | No, it is a loud sound | Yes, it is a tiny step | *No, an abyss is a very deep hole or gap
